From c9e3e2fe884cc5bda0a367d2cae83de588fe2142 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:05:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: usb_kbd_hid: don't fall back to control endpoint on
 a benign interrupt poll timeout

usb_kbd_probe()'s one-shot interrupt endpoint test poll treated any
negative return, including -EAGAIN and -ETIMEDOUT, as proof the
interrupt endpoint was broken, permanently switching do_poll to the
control endpoint fallback for the rest of the session.

At probe time nothing has been pressed yet, so -EAGAIN/-ETIMEDOUT
from that one-shot test is the expected, normal result, not a sign of
a broken endpoint. Since this check ran unconditionally on any
negative return, it triggered on essentially every boot.

The control endpoint fallback cannot work on this device: the
keyboard firmware's GET_REPORT handler (pocket-reform-keyboard-fw) is
an unimplemented stub that always returns 0, so control endpoint
polling can never see live data. Falling back to it on a benign
timeout meant the keyboard was routed to a dead path on essentially
every boot, before real interrupt polling was ever given a chance.

Fix: only fall back on a genuine error, not -EAGAIN/-ETIMEDOUT.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index 9483835a07..332368d518 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -196,10 +196,16 @@ static int usb_kbd_probe(struct usb_device *usbdev,
 	data->intpktsize = min(usb_maxpacket(usbdev, data->intpipe),
 			       USB_KBD_BOOT_REPORT_SIZE);
 	data->intinterval = data->ep->bInterval;
-	/* test polling via interrupt endpoint */
+	/*
+	 * Test polling via interrupt endpoint. -EAGAIN / -ETIMEDOUT here just
+	 * mean no report was pending at this instant (normal at probe time,
+	 * before any key has been touched) and does not indicate the
+	 * interrupt endpoint is broken. Only a genuine error should trigger
+	 * the control endpoint fallback.
+	 */
 	data->do_poll = usb_kbd_int_poll;
 	ret = data->do_poll(data);
-	if (ret < 0) {
+	if (ret < 0 && ret != -EAGAIN && ret != -ETIMEDOUT) {
 		/* fall back to polling via control enpoint */
 		data->do_poll = usb_kbd_cnt_poll;
 		usb_set_idle(usbdev,
-- 
